TCC(1)

NAME
    tcc - compile C programs with TinyCC

SYNOPSIS
    tcc [options] file ...

DESCRIPTION
    tcc is the SmallOS build of TinyCC. It can compile small C programs inside
    the system image. By default it uses the installed SmallOS guest sysroot,
    with headers in /usr/include and runtime objects/libraries in /usr/lib.

    The shipped compiler is intended for experiments and demos, not for
    rebuilding the whole operating system from inside SmallOS.

FILES
    /usr/include
        Public libc, POSIX, SmallOS, kernel UAPI, and compatibility headers.

    /usr/lib/crt0.o
        Startup object for hosted main() programs.

    /usr/lib/libc.a, /usr/lib/libm.a, /usr/lib/libposix.a
        SmallOS runtime libraries used by guest builds.

    /usr/share/examples/tinycc
        Example C source files.

EXAMPLES
    cd /var/tmp
    tcc -o tccsysroot /usr/share/examples/tinycc/tccsysroot.c
    /var/tmp/tccsysroot
    tcc -o tccposix /usr/share/examples/tinycc/tccposix.c
    /var/tmp/tccposix

    tcc -nostdlib -o tccmini /usr/share/examples/tinycc/tccmini.c
    /var/tmp/tccmini

SEE ALSO
    compiler_demo(1), shell(1), smallos(7)
